  "prompt": "A VAT-registered exporter sells 100% abroad. Can it obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, a VAT-registered exporter must ensure that they maintain proper documentation of their input VAT and the related purchases. They can file for a refund or tax credit with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) by submitting the necessary documents, including the VAT returns and proof of export sales. This process helps exporters manage their cash flow effectively by recovering the VAT they have paid, which is particularly beneficial for businesses operating in a zero-rated export environment.",
